WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:11.809
Speaker 1: We are now getting the expert testimony
of the not smartest son of the former President

00:00:11.809 --> 00:00:12.809
Donald Trump.

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:14.320
I'm talking about Eric Trump.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:21.020
Eric Trump went on Fox News's Hannity program
to try to defend his dad and attack Joe Biden

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:22.529
on the topic of Ukraine.

00:00:22.529 --> 00:00:29.100
And now at this point, it sort of seems pointless
in the sense that Joe Biden has an almost

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:34.320
60 percent approval on his handling of Ukraine,
which in a country as polarized as the United

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.820
States when 60 percent of the country believes
are doing a good job.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:39.820
That's pretty overwhelming.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:45.399
Sadly, in this polarized state of affairs,
Trump never had 60 percent approval on anything

00:00:45.399 --> 00:00:48.080
that he oversaw while he was president.

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.460
And they clearly know what they're trying
to run interference for Trump.

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:57.850
But remember, Trump withheld military aid
to Ukraine, hoping it would force Zelensky

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:00.620
to start providing dirt on Joe Biden.

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:05.679
Thanks to that little strategy being outed,
Trump ultimately had to release the military

00:01:05.679 --> 00:01:06.679
aid to Ukraine.

00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:12.359
So anyway, Eric Trump talks to Sean Hannity,
and it's all completely crazy.

00:01:12.359 --> 00:01:16.789
It's a delusional fantasy world understanding
of how Trump and foreign policy co-existed,

00:01:16.789 --> 00:01:22.689
and this is the Trumpian sort of analysis
that counts as analysis in their world in

00:01:22.689 --> 00:01:23.689
which they live.

00:01:23.689 --> 00:01:27.509
Speaker 2: Listen, my father would call up
and he would have said, Vladimir, don't even

00:01:27.509 --> 00:01:28.509
think about it.

00:01:28.509 --> 00:01:29.829
Don't even try us.

00:01:29.829 --> 00:01:31.909
I'm telling you, it's not going to work out
very well for you, right?

00:01:31.909 --> 00:01:36.279
Speaker 1: So this is the idea that Trump
was really, really tough on Putin and that

00:01:36.279 --> 00:01:37.749
Putin respected Trump.

00:01:37.749 --> 00:01:40.280
Now you can say a lot of things about Putin.

00:01:40.280 --> 00:01:43.969
I don't think he really cares about the welfare
of individual Russians.

00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:48.799
He cares about, you know, furthering his plans
for a sort of new USSR.

00:01:48.799 --> 00:01:49.999
And that's his priority.

00:01:49.999 --> 00:01:52.419
Putin's ruthless and brutal.

00:01:52.419 --> 00:01:53.529
He disappears.

00:01:53.529 --> 00:01:56.700
Dissidents, he disappears, you know, disappears.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:02.069
And by that, I mean kills and sometimes unjustly
imprisons media people who don't agree.

00:02:02.069 --> 00:02:03.989
You can say all that stuff about Putin.

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:06.489
But Putin is way smarter than Trump.

00:02:06.489 --> 00:02:07.989
There is no doubt about that.

00:02:07.989 --> 00:02:13.819
And there is no way in hell that Putin was
intimidated in any way by Donald Trump.

00:02:13.819 --> 00:02:15.120
Let's go to the next clip.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:17.620
Speaker 2: By the way, my father had a great
relationship with Putin.

00:02:17.620 --> 00:02:21.580
We know all the while he's sending thousands
of javelin missiles to the Ukraine.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:27.000
Is that really made, by the way,
Speaker 1: they still are on the Ukraine thing?

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:29.019
I mean,
Speaker 2: Biden has no relationship with

00:02:29.019 --> 00:02:32.280
Putin, and he's literally sending blankets
for Ukraine.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:37.370
It's, you know, again, Sean, it's
Speaker 1: so these are, of course, lies Biden

00:02:37.370 --> 00:02:42.400
and the U.S. has have sent significant military
aid to Ukraine.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.879
Remember that the aide, Eric Trump is referring
to his dad sending was aid that Trump initially

00:02:47.879 --> 00:02:53.519
withheld because he was trying to push Zelensky
to announce that they were investigating Joe

00:02:53.519 --> 00:02:54.890
and Hunter Biden.

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.700
He ultimately released the aid.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:03.950
But again, importantly, a good relationship
with Putin comes when Putin sees that you're

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:06.650
a joke, when Putin sees that you're a patsy.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:10.490
And that's exactly what Putin saw in Donald
Trump.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:16.330
Here's one last clip of Eric Trump's incisive
and principled analysis of geopolitics by.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:20.709
Speaker 2: Well, Mr. Putin was in with the
KGB.

00:03:20.709 --> 00:03:24.439
He can read people and he could tell that
Donald Trump was a very strong person, right?

00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:25.739
Speaker 1: Right.

00:03:25.739 --> 00:03:26.739
No wrong.

00:03:26.739 --> 00:03:29.440
And again, 90 percent of that sentence is
right.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.030
Putin was in the KGB.

00:03:32.030 --> 00:03:38.299
Putin can read people, and he can tell that
Donald Trump was a very weak person.

00:03:38.299 --> 00:03:44.109
I mean, remember Trump coming out in Helsinki
and saying, Listen, I asked him, Did you hack

00:03:44.109 --> 00:03:45.109
us?

00:03:45.109 --> 00:03:46.420
Did you hack the U.S.?

00:03:46.420 --> 00:03:50.730
And he said no, and he said it very strongly,
and I believe him.

00:03:50.730 --> 00:03:51.799
That's what Putin signed.

00:03:51.799 --> 00:03:57.180
Trump, Trump is a patsy, so nobody ever said
Eric was the smart one.

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:04.529
But now, just obviously, I mean, just laughably
unbelievable claims about Trump's handling

00:04:04.529 --> 00:05:11.620
of geopolitics, foreign relations, Russia

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:18.210
and Ukraine.

